ange in the user’s location, when the user tracking mode","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes, or when the viewport changes."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"During user interaction with the map, this method may be called many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"times to update the user location annotation. Therefore, your implementation of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this method should be as lightweight as possible to avoid negatively affecting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"performance."}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNUserLocation":{"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnuserlocation","title":"MLNUserLocation","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNUserLocation","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The MLNUserLocation class defines a specific type of annotation that identifies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user’s current location. You do not create instances of this class","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directly. Instead, you retrieve an existing ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNUserLocation","type":"reference"},{"text":" object from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userLocation"},{"text":" property of the map view displayed in your application.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"MLNUserLocation","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNUserLocationAnnotationView/update":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNUserLocationAnnotationView\/update","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnuserlocationannotationvie